    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a challenging slate today, navigating several elite opposing arms that compress our overall efficiency. The clear engine for our offense is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who carries the day\u2019s highest projection at 74.55. He benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Nick Martinez, whose 4.63 xERA offers a high ceiling for run production, bolstered by a +14% platoon advantage. **Kyle Tucker** (67.73) and **Heliot Ramos** (65.81) follow close behind; both are strong starts primarily due to their ability to exploit Martinez\u2019s soft contact profile, with **Heliot Ramos** specifically seeing a 15% boost from the SP skill adjustment. While **Jackson Merrill** (56.70) remains a core piece of our lineup, his neutral matchup status keeps him slightly below the \"Strong\" threshold, though he remains locked in for his daily stability.\n\nIn the middle of the order, we are cautious with **Drake Baldwin** (44.96), **Liam Hicks** (40.16), and **Miguel Vargas** (40.49). These players are facing formidable resistance from Tyler Glasnow and Espino, respectively. Specifically, **Miguel Vargas** is navigating a brutal matchup against the 2.51 xERA of Espino, and while his order position (#2) provides some salvage value, his status is effectively \"marginal.\" Our most difficult bench decision involved **Dominic Smith** (37.51), who fell just shy of the start against Tyler Glasnow. While **Dominic Smith** offered potential platoon upside, the optimizer penalized him for an unfavorable #8 spot in the lineup and the general difficulty of facing Glasnow, ultimately opting to stick with the higher-ceiling profiles in our primary OF slots. \n\nRisk management remains paramount, as several of our starters\u2014including **Drake Baldwin**, **Liam Hicks**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**\u2014are subject to \"Lineup Pending\" status. Should these assumed batting orders shift unfavorably, particularly for the likes of **Luis Lara** (48.53) or **Brayan Rocchio** (43.10), their scores could slide further into the \"Below floor\" range. We are currently without the services of **Gunnar Henderson** due to an off-day, and remain depleted in the utility ranks as **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** continue their recovery on the IL.",
